course: dictionary
lesson: 10502
title: Twelve and the dozen
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Twelve is the number 12. It comes straight after eleven, so when you count on from eleven, the next number is twelve.
explain: A dozen means twelve, so a dozen eggs is twelve eggs. A year has twelve months, and a clock face shows twelve hours.
explain: Twelve turns up in lots of places. «Twelve pairs of ribs curve round from the spine like a cage.» Count the pairs and you get twelve.
explain: Other languages have their own words for numbers. Sashko shouts «dvanAdtsyat!» when he means twelve. The word changes, but the number stays the same.
fact: Twelve is the number 12, and it is one more than eleven.
fact: A dozen is twelve, so «eggs are sold by the dozen» means you buy twelve eggs.
fact: A year has twelve months, and a clock face shows twelve hours.
fact: «Twelve o'clock» is noon or midnight.
fact: A foot has twelve inches.
exercise: What number is one more than eleven? | Nine | Thirteen | Ten | *Twelve
exercise: A dozen eggs means how many eggs? | *Twelve | Twenty | Ten | Six
exercise: How many months are in a year? | Ten | Eleven | *Twelve | Thirteen
test: On a clock face, how many hours are shown? | *Twelve | Twenty-four | Ten | Six
test: Twelve inches make one what? | Mile | Metre | *Foot | Yard
exam: Sashko's word for twelve is «dvanAdtsyat». If a team has a dozen players, how many players is that? | Fourteen | Ten | Eleven | *Twelve
